
```rust
Affordance::Edge(edges) =>
    Gesture::Resize { edges },
```

as the single compositor-controlled route.

---

# 17. Do not change client-requested resize behavior

This distinction matters.

Wayland applications can send:

```text
xdg_toplevel.resize
```

with conventional directions such as:

```text
left
right
top
bottom
top_left
...
```

Do not reinterpret those.

A client asking for:

```text
RIGHT
```

should continue to get a one-axis right-edge resize.

The new two-axis side semantics should apply specifically to **TemplarOS compositor-owned pointer affordances**.

So:

```text
client resize protocol
        ↓
honor requested edges exactly
```

while:

```text
Templar perimeter press
        ↓
derive two edges from side + midpoint
```

This keeps protocol behavior correct.

---
